WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:02.961
Easy Folk Tales. Little Red Riding Hood.

00:00:02.961 --> 00:00:07.012
There was once a little girl who always wore a red coat with a hood.

00:00:07.012 --> 00:00:09.554
Everybody called her Little Red Riding Hood.

00:00:09.554 --> 00:00:12.679
One day her mother said, "Your grandmother is sick.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:15.145
Take her this cake and this bottle of milk.

00:00:15.145 --> 00:00:18.741
Go straight there, and do not talk to anyone on the way."

00:00:18.741 --> 00:00:21.684
The grandmother lived on the other side of the forest.

00:00:21.684 --> 00:00:24.960
On the path, Little Red Riding Hood met a wolf.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.586
She did not know that wolves were dangerous.

00:00:27.586 --> 00:00:30.874
"Where are you going, little girl?" asked the wolf.

00:00:30.874 --> 00:00:34.976
"To my grandmother's house, at the end of this path," she said.

00:00:34.976 --> 00:00:36.669
The wolf had an idea.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.599
"Look at all these beautiful flowers," he said.

00:00:39.599 --> 00:00:41.813
"Why not pick some for your grandmother?"

00:00:41.813 --> 00:00:46.315
While the girl picked flowers, the wolf ran to the grandmother's house.

00:00:46.315 --> 00:00:47.809
He knocked on the door.

00:00:47.809 --> 00:00:51.845
The grandmother thought it was the little girl and told him to come in.

00:00:51.845 --> 00:00:56.278
When she saw the wolf, she was so afraid that she hid in the cupboard.

00:00:56.278 --> 00:00:59.745
The wolf put on her night clothes and got into her bed.

00:00:59.745 --> 00:01:02.210
Soon Little Red Riding Hood came in.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:04.564
Her grandmother looked very strange.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:07.779
"Grandmother, what big ears you have," she said.

00:01:07.779 --> 00:01:10.332
"All the better to hear you with, my dear."

00:01:10.332 --> 00:01:12.788
"Grandmother, what big eyes you have."

00:01:12.788 --> 00:01:14.611
"All the better to see you with."

00:01:14.611 --> 00:01:17.111
"Grandmother, what big teeth you have!"

00:01:17.111 --> 00:01:21.946
"All the better to eat you with!" cried the wolf, and he jumped out of the bed.

00:01:21.946 --> 00:01:23.270
The girl screamed.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:26.094
A man who was cutting wood near the house heard her.

00:01:26.094 --> 00:01:31.756
He ran in with his axe, and the wolf jumped through the window and ran away as fast as he could.

00:01:31.756 --> 00:01:36.581
The grandmother came out of the cupboard, and the three of them sat down to eat the cake.

00:01:36.581 --> 00:01:39.884
And Little Red Riding Hood never talked to a wolf again.
